The expression ``Tr^p % I'' computes the normal form for the p-th power of the
trace Tr with respect to the Gröbner basis of I. The expression ``for p from 1
to 10 do'' specifies a for loop that executes the following expression, ``print
(Tr^p % I)'', with 10 consecutive values of p. For more information on such
loops see *note for: (Macaulay2Doc)for, or type:

+--------------+
|viewHelp "for"|
+--------------+

Here we have put quotes around ``for'' because ``for'' is a keyword in the
Macaulay2 language.  (In general, it's always safe to use quotes with
viewHelp.)

